> what is the range of x squared for a signed byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x^2
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i8:
  -127..121   (44 distinct values)
  values: -127, -124, -119, -112..-111, -103, -95, -92, -87, -79, -71, -63, -60, -55, -47, -39, -31, -28, -23, -15, -7, 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, ...
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is the wrap of x squared for u8 x?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x^2
  ucas: wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  no wrapping or rounding operations
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 240 points, e.g. x=16
      exact for: 0..15
  over all 256 points of the domain
> the sum of a and b
  ucas: it(a, b) = a + b
  ucas: show it
it(a: real, b: real) = a + b
  -> real
> what is 2 + 2?
  ucas: 2 + 2
4
> factor x squared minus 1
  ucas: factor x^2 - 1
factor x^2 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> solve x squared = 4 for x
  ucas: solve x^2 == 4 for x
solve x^2 == 4 for x
  note: a coefficient is a rounded decimal (numbers in expressions are doubles), so the solutions are approximate
  x = -2
  x = 2
  check: each solution substituted (2 values): residual 0
